<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gutasaga</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Guta saga</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Gutasaga is a short Old Gutnish account of the early history of Gotland, written down in the thirteenth century and preserved with the island's law, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gutalag">Gutalag</a>. It tells of the legendary settler Tjelvar, who brought fire to the island, of the emigration of part of its people, and of the treaty by which Gotland paid a yearly tribute to the Swedish king in return for protection.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gutasaga.jpg" alt="Gutasaga" width="320" height="340" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Berig · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Snake-witch.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
